## 4. Future Tasks (Do Not Do These Yet)

Do not work on these tasks until the main code is stable.

- **Self-Healing Code:** Make the system fix itself when it finds a bug.
- **Time-Travel Memory:** Build a way to undo changes if the system crashes.
- **Auto-Delete Large Files:** Make the system auto-delete files that are larger than 256 lines.
- **Safe Code Sharing:** Build a way to safely share code with other projects.
- **Math Proofs:** Use math to prove the code is safe before it runs.
- **Hardware Limits:** Limit how much memory and CPU the code can use.
- **Security Signatures:** Sign the code so we know it is safe to run.
- **Safe Database Writes:** Test database writes in a safe space before saving them.
- **AI Code Builder:** Add an AI to write code automatically.
- **GPU Support:** Make the code run on graphics cards.
- **Live Code Updates:** Update the code while it is running without stopping it.
- **Fast Memory Layout:** Change how data is saved in memory to make it run faster.
- **Small Error Messages:** Make error messages small so the AI can read them easily.
- **Exact Code Patching:** Change the code patching tool to change specific parts of the code.
- **AI Code Reader:** Add a tool to let the AI read code structures quickly.
- **Code Mixing:** Let the system mix different parts of code to find the best version.
- **Web Browser:** Build a safe web browser.
- **Operating System Kernel:** Build a safe base for an operating system.
- **Direct Disk Saving:** Save data directly to the disk without extra steps.
- **Cross-Language Merging:** Merge our code with Rust code to make it faster.
- **Safe Threading:** Let the code use multiple CPU cores safely.

---

## 5. Completed Tasks

We completed a large security audit on August 11, 2026. We fixed all 50 critical security holes found in the audit. The system is now much more secure.
